# OFFCUT AGENT — configuration
#
# Every value here has a working default. Copy to .env only when you need to
# change one; `pnpm setup && pnpm dev` runs with this file absent.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Storage
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# SQLite, relative to packages/core/prisma. This is the shipped default and
# matches §4: "the first release is local".
DATABASE_URL="file:../.data/offcut.db"

# PostgreSQL instead — see README, "Moving to PostgreSQL". Changing this line is
# not sufficient on its own: Prisma needs the provider changed in the schema too.
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://offcut:offcut@localhost:5432/offcut?schema=public"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# API
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

PORT=4000

# Origin allowed to send credentialed requests. Must be the exact console origin.
WEB_ORIGIN="http://localhost:3000"

# Signs console sessions.
#
# REQUIRED in production — the API refuses to start without it when
# NODE_ENV=production. In development a random secret is generated once and
# cached in apps/api/.data/session-secret so restarts do not sign everyone out.
#
# Generate one with:  node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
# OFFCUT_JWT_SECRET="replace-me-with-64-hex-characters"

NODE_ENV=development

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Console
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Where the Next.js app proxies /api/* to. Keeps the session cookie first-party.
OFFCUT_API_URL="http://localhost:4000"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# $OFFCUT token
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Launch day is one edit. Set the contract address here (or in
# apps/web/src/lib/token.ts) and every surface that mentions the token switches
# from "not yet published" to the live state on its own.
#
# A value that is not a valid EVM address (0x + 40 hex characters) is NOT
# displayed — the page shows a visible warning instead. People copy these
# strings into wallets, so a convincing-looking wrong one is the failure mode
# worth engineering against.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_OFFCUT_CONTRACT_ADDRESS="0x..."

# Explorer address page, without a trailing address. The explorer button only
# renders once this is set — a link that 404s on launch day is worse than none.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_OFFCUT_EXPLORER_URL="https://explorer.example.com/address/"

# Optional link to the launch venue listing.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_OFFCUT_VENUE_URL=""

# No price, volume or chart feed is configured, and none is built. §1 puts
# market monitoring outside the product boundary.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Reward publisher (apps/publisher)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# A separate process. Nothing below is read by the core, the API, the MCP server
# or the console, and none of them starts any worse for all of it being unset -
# the publisher is the only thing here that signs a transaction.
#
# It settles each closed period and publishes the cumulative Merkle root to
# OffcutRewards. It skips the transaction when the root has not moved, so quiet
# hours cost nothing.

# The deployed OffcutRewards PROXY, not the implementation behind it. Required.
# OFFCUT_CONTRACT_ADDRESS="0x..."

# mainnet (4663) unless this says testnet (46630). Everything that touches money
# is exercised on the testnet first.
# OFFCUT_NETWORK="testnet"

# Override the RPC endpoint. Unset, it follows OFFCUT_NETWORK.
# OFFCUT_RPC_URL=""

# The publisher key, one way or the other - NEVER both, because a stale variable
# silently beating a freshly rotated file is a service signing as an address the
# contract stopped accepting. It holds no tokens, only enough gas: a thief who
# takes it can misdirect future rewards but cannot withdraw, upgrade or pause.
# Prefer the file; an environment variable is visible to every child process and
# to anything that dumps the environment on a crash.
# OFFCUT_PUBLISHER_KEY_FILE="/run/secrets/offcut-publisher.key"
# OFFCUT_PUBLISHER_KEY="0x..."

# Rehearsal: does everything except send the transaction. Accruals are still
# recorded and proof files are still written, so it is not read-only - but any
# key will do, funded or not.
# OFFCUT_PUBLISHER_DRY_RUN=1

# Seconds to wait past a period boundary before reading it, so the window is
# settled rather than racing the database's clock. Default 15.
# OFFCUT_PUBLISHER_TICK_LAG_SECONDS=15

# Seconds to wait for a receipt before giving up on a publication. The next
# period republishes a root that supersedes it, so this is a delay, not a loss.
# Default 120.
# OFFCUT_PUBLISHER_CONFIRM_SECONDS=120

# How much may be emitted, and how a period's pool is split, is NOT set here:
# OFFCUT_REWARD_* is read by @offcut/rewards, which the API reads too. One
# parser, one opinion about emission.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MCP server
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# An agent key, minted in the console under Agents → New agent. Shown once.
# The MCP server reads its identity from here and from nowhere else: a model
# cannot talk its way into another identity (§3.2).
# OFFCUT_API_KEY="offcut_sk_..."

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Backups (OPEN-5, answered: 30 days)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# How long snapshots are kept before `pnpm backup` prunes them.
# OFFCUT_BACKUP_RETENTION_DAYS=30

# Where the SQLite file, the deletion ledger and the snapshots all live.
# OFFCUT_DATA_DIR="./packages/core/.data"

# The deletion ledger is NEVER pruned, whatever the retention is. It holds no
# record content — only which record was deleted and when — and it is what makes
# restoring an old snapshot safe: deletions recorded after the snapshot was taken
# are replayed on top of it, so nothing you deleted comes back.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model summaries — the OPTIONAL module of §9
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Off by default and off per workspace until an OWNER turns it on in the console.
# Setting this key alone sends nothing anywhere.
#
# Writing, merging, deduplication and recall never use a model. This module only
# adds proposed connections and possible conflicts on top, and it cannot change a
# record, resolve a conflict, or widen who can see anything.
#
# Get a key at https://openrouter.ai/keys
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-...

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Debugging
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Logs every SQL query issued by the core.
# OFFCUT_DEBUG=1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately absent
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The core reads no RPC URL, no wallet, no chain id and no private key. It runs
# without any of them — invariant 10 — and the acceptance suite fails if that
# ever stops being true. The publisher section above is the one place in this
# file where a chain and a key appear, and it is a process of its own: unset
# every variable in it and the memory system is unaffected.
#
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY above is the one external credential, and it powers ONLY the
# optional module of §9. Every core operation works with it unset.

# Where an INSTALLED copy of @offcut/core keeps its store. Unset: ~/.offcut/offcut.db.
# Inside this checkout DATABASE_URL above is what counts; installed copies ignore it.
# OFFCUT_DATABASE_URL="file:/absolute/path/offcut.db"
